course: dictionary
lesson: 9029
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Ollie slammed his door shouting "it's only paper!"» Slam here means shut hard and loudly, and the shouting tells you he was cross.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «Standing up and walking away is safer than hitting or slamming things in anger.» Slamming things here means banging or throwing them down hard. Does that make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Slam can also be a noun: a slam is the loud sound of something shutting or hitting hard. Sport and the news use slam in other ways too, so always read the words around it before you decide.
fact: «Slam» means to shut something hard and loudly, like a door, window or lid.
fact: To slam something down or into something means to put or push it with great force.
fact: To slam into something means to crash into it.
fact: Informally, to slam someone means to criticise them strongly, as in the news.
fact: A slam dunk in basketball is when a player jumps and pushes the ball down through the hoop.
exercise: What does slammed mean in «Slammed doors crush thousands of children's fingers every year»? | Counted carefully | *Shut hard and loudly | Painted in bright colours | Opened very gently
exercise: «Standing up and walking away is safer than hitting or slamming things in anger.» Here, slamming means | Sorting things into neat piles | Putting things down gently | Singing loudly | *Banging or throwing things down with great force
exercise: In basketball, what is a slam dunk? | *A player jumps and pushes the ball down through the hoop | A ball that bounces off the floor | Shooting from a long way out | Passing the ball to a teammate
test: In a story, «she slammed the door» tells the reader the character is | Lost | Bored | Tidying up | *Angry or upset
test: In the news, «slammed» means | *Criticised strongly | Cooked | Hidden | Painted
exam: In «slam on the brakes», slam means | Shut a box quietly | Speak softly | *Press or push with great force | Clean the windows
